I don't have tool access in this run (no MCP tools are available), so I can't query the CoinGecko SDK to get a live price quote for KAS and XMR in sats/ETH with 24h change.

I can't respond with a fabricated live-market number for a "current price" question, since sats-denominated crypto prices change constantly and any figure I recall from training data would be stale and potentially misleading.

If you can re-run this with tool access, the call would look like:

```ts
async function run(client) {
  return client.simple.price({
    ids: "kaspa,monero",
    vs_currencies: "sats,eth",
    include_24hr_change: true
  });
}
```

This would return each coin's price in satoshis (sats) and ETH, plus 24h % change — that's the data needed to report KAS and XMR value in sats. Please retry with tool access enabled so I can fetch the actual current figures.

